## Roadmap handoff

**The actual CPU software-candidate acceptance blocker is closed.** Gate 5 as
a whole is not yet closed. First correct the Source regression-test isolation
without re-executing the accepted CPU workload; then integrate the accepted
immutable candidate with the existing guardian and worker/supervisor admission
path. The latter was already the remaining step in v0.49; no new stand-in gate
is added here.

A fresh local-only `tests/test_sft_cpu_version_lookup_v3.py` prepares the test
correction, SHA-256
`b65ac4456be9dce2af6b9c02c247ec9f0b1778b7f6cd49bcc052f30ad7296917`.
All 22 focused tests and exact-file Ruff pass. A tiny synthetic module registry
reproduces the published guard's false rejection without importing ML; the
successor allows preexisting synthetic ML entries, still rejects a native-probe
entry with a fixed message, and verifies the test's stdlib-only imports and
absence of dynamic native execution through AST. No test is silently skipped.
The published v2 test and all acceptance sources remain byte-identical.
The full selected isolated local suite, including this successor, passes:
436 tests in 0.507s under `-S -B`. This does not substitute for a fresh Source-CI
result on a properly integrated test correction.

The v3 test is not wired into or published to Source CI, so it does not erase
the failed run. Updating the current v2 test path directly would match the new
CPU workflow's push filter and must not be done as an unplanned acceptance
retry. A separately scoped Source-only integration/publication must first
prevent that unintended CPU run while preserving the accepted commit/image.

Dedicated real-host binding, the original pretrained S3 checkpoint restoration,
exact data relocation and explicitly approved H100/CUDA checks remain downstream.
This CPU software image is not a replacement for that pretrained model backup.
No S3/SSH access, real checkpoint/data read, GPU/instance operation, real-model
inference/SFT, dataset seal or promotion occurred.

Production eligibility, real SFT permission, real-host admission, complete
dynamic closure, private integration and full-CI claims remain false. This
receipt does not authorize another remote run or those downstream actions.
